CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'val != val2'
#330: FILE: drivers/iommu/amd_iommu_init.c:1149:
+	if ((iommu_pc_get_set_reg(iommu, 0, 0, 0, &val, true)) ||
+	    (iommu_pc_get_set_reg(iommu, 0, 0, 0, &val2, false)) ||
 	    (val != val2)) {

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

